<diagram name="Notation and assumptions" id="_RQ4NZbv8J6uawSwuvyP">
<mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2100" pageHeight="660" math="0" shadow="0" background="#FFFFFF">
<root>
<mxCell id="0"/>
<mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
<mxCell id="ntitle" value="ZK-SNARK EHR WORKFLOW — NOTATION AND ASSUMPTIONS" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFE082;strokeColor=#C8A415;fontSize=30;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#3E2C00;arcSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
<mxGeometry x="60" y="40" width="900" height="56" as="geometry"/>
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="note0" value="<b>The relations being proved</b><br><br>Attribute (single subject):<br>R₁(u, w) = 1 ⟺ H(w ‖ s) = u ∧ a ≤ w ≤ b<br>or, for set membership: H(w ‖ s) = u ∧ Merkle(ℓ, path, rt) = 1<br><br>Analysis (cohort):<br>R₂ adds inclusion of the condition and the treatment in the authorised sets rtₘ, rtₜ, and membership of the drawn sample i in the dataset rt<sub>D</sub> — all four roots folded into the single signal c<sub>rt</sub>." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=20;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=20;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;fontColor=#3E2C00;" vertex="1" parent="1">
<mxGeometry x="60" y="140" width="640" height="360" as="geometry"/>
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="note1" value="<b>What each property rests on</b><br><br>Completeness: R(u, w) = 1 ⇒ Ver(vₖ, u, π) = 1<br>Soundness: without w, an accepting π is infeasible to produce<br>Zero-knowledge: π is simulatable from u alone, so it leaks nothing about w<br>Setup: phase 1 needs one honest contributor over τ; phase 2 needs one honest ρᵣ — here supplied by the enclave and erased<br>Hardware: trust reduces to the pinned measurement M*, which anyone can reproduce and compare" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=20;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=20;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;fontColor=#3E2C00;" vertex="1" parent="1">
<mxGeometry x="740" y="140" width="640" height="360" as="geometry"/>
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="note2" value="<b>Choice of proof system</b><br><br>Deployed — Groth16: |π| = 3 group elements ≈ 192 B, verification cost constant, but phase 2 must be repeated for every relation R.<br><br>Universal alternatives — PLONK and Marlin: a single updatable reference string serves every R, so phase 2 disappears, at the cost of a larger proof (≈ 672 B and ≈ 880 B).<br><br>The trade-off is one ceremony per relation against proof size and verification gas." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=20;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=20;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;fontColor=#3E2C00;" vertex="1" parent="1">
<mxGeometry x="1420" y="140" width="640" height="360" as="geometry"/>
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="notation" value="<b>Notation</b>&nbsp;&nbsp; R : relation &nbsp;&nbsp; w : private witness &nbsp;&nbsp; u : public statement &nbsp;&nbsp; s : salt &nbsp;&nbsp; H : hash &nbsp;&nbsp; srs₁ : universal reference string &nbsp;&nbsp; pₖ / vₖ : prover / verifier key &nbsp;&nbsp; ρ : setup secret &nbsp;&nbsp; π : proof &nbsp;&nbsp; σ : enclave signature &nbsp;&nbsp; rt : Merkle root &nbsp;&nbsp; |Q| : queue size" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#9CB8D1;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=20;align=left;spacingLeft=16;fontColor=#33475B;arcSize=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
<mxGeometry x="60" y="536" width="1960" height="64" as="geometry"/>
</mxCell>
</root>
</mxGraphModel>
</diagram>
</mxfile>